# Chromebook Audio Fix (Arch Linux)
Quick guide for restoring audio support on Chromebook devices running Arch Linux or Arch-based distributions.

Install required tools:
"sudo pacman -Syu git python alsa-utils"

Clone the repository:
"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/WeirdTreeThing/chromebook-linux-audio"

Navigate to the directory:
"cd chromebook-linux-audio"

Run the setup script:
"./setup-audio"

Reboot the system to apply changes:
"reboot"

# Hardware & Testing Environment

This procedure was tested and confirmed working on the following setup:

* **Device:** Samsung Chromebook Go
* **Board Name / HWID:** `SASUKE`
* **CPU:** Intel Celeron N4500
* **RAM / Storage:** 8 GB RAM / 64 GB eMMC
* **Firmware:** Full ROM UEFI Firmware unlocked via [MrChromebox.tech](https://mrchromebox.tech/) script.
* **OS:** Arch Linux / CachyOS (Kernel 6.x+)

> **Note:** Unlocking the coreboot/UEFI firmware via MrChromebox script is a required step prior to installing Linux and applying audio patches on Chromebooks with Jasper Lake architecture (`SASUKE`).
Script provided by WeirdTreeThing/chromebook-linux-audio.

